   "daf": "59a",
   "sentenceId": 13,
   "he": "וְשֶׁל מִזְבֵּחַ הַחִיצוֹן הָיָה שׁוֹפֵךְ עַל יְסוֹד דְּרוֹמִית. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: יְסוֹד הַמִּזְבֵּחַ — זֶה יְסוֹד דְּרוֹמִית. אַתָּה אוֹמֵר יְסוֹד דְּרוֹמִית, אוֹ אֵינוֹ אֶלָּא יְסוֹד מַעֲרָבִית?",
   "en": "§ The mishna further taught: «And he would pour» the remaining blood after the blood of an offering was sprinkled «on the outer altar, on its southern base. The Sages taught» in a baraita: «“The base of the altar”» (Leviticus 4:30), which is mentioned with regard to pouring the remainder of the blood of an individual offering, «is the southern base.» Do «you say» it is «the southern base? Or perhaps that is not» the case, but «rather» it is «the western base?»"
  }
